1
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Come in.

2
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:50,920
Mr. Li, the advisor asked me
to bring this to you.

3
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:53,240
Thank you.

4
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:54,720
Zheng Yu.

5
00:01:58,240 --> 00:02:01,280
I know you and Yanzhou are good friends.

6
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:02,600
Can you talk to him?

7
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:05,960
Well, there's a research institute
in Germany

8
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:08,560
working on a cancer cell research project.

9
00:02:08,639 --> 00:02:12,160
They've opened internship positions
to college students worldwide.

10
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:14,960
I think he should give it a try.

11
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:18,200
You should talk to him about it.

12
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:21,520
I couldn't get through to him.

13
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:23,320
He didn't agree to it?

14
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:26,520
That's normal.

15
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:29,160
This doesn't align
with his chosen area of research.

16
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:34,240
However,

17
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:36,640
he's still young

18
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:39,600
and doesn't know
that he has other options.

19
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:43,600
Mr. Li,

20
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:46,760
as his friend, I think
I should respect his opinion.

21
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,000
Okay.

22
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:56,920
There are three common methods
for separating plasmid DNA.

23
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,320
The alkaline lysis method,

24
00:02:58,400 --> 00:02:59,720
the boiling lysis method,

25
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:02,960
and the detergent lysis method.

26
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:04,120
That's about it.

27
00:03:40,920 --> 00:03:41,800
What is it?

28
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,560
Nothing.

29
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:45,840
I just thought

30
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:47,440
you looked like a teacher.

31
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:48,760
No, wait.

32
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:50,160
You <i>are </i>a teacher.

33
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:52,440
Ms. Zheng.

34
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:57,640
Are you done cleaning up?
Do you have time for jokes?

35
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:00,640
Ms. Zheng,

36
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:01,800
I'll be done soon.

37
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:06,840
Chen Yanzhou,

38
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:08,960
Fu Yu is looking for you outside.

39
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,400
Okay.

40
00:04:11,480 --> 00:04:12,680
I'm stepping out.

41
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:21,800
Why is Fu Yu here?

42
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:23,480
I heard she's pursuing Yanzhou.

43
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:26,000
Isn't she going abroad?

44
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:27,600
Why pursue anyone?

45
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:28,640
In our field,

46
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:30,240
plenty of people study abroad.

47
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:32,560
Chen Yanzhou will
eventually go abroad too.

48
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:34,800
They seem like a good match.

49
00:04:34,880 --> 00:04:36,280
I'm hungry. Let's go eat.

50
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:37,200
Sure.

51
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:41,560
DUAN SHENGYANG

52
00:04:48,840 --> 00:04:50,680
Hello, Shengyang.

53
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:06,560
Where is she?

54
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:13,160
Shengyang.

55
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:15,000
There you are. Come on.

56
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:16,160
Let's eat first.

57
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:17,960
No, thanks. What is this about?

58
00:05:18,640 --> 00:05:21,040
I'm starving after my group meeting.

59
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:23,160
I've got my boss's card.

60
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:25,440
He doesn't hand it over often.
Let's feast.

61
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:34,280
What would you like?

62
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:35,200
Noodles.

63
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:39,040
Find a place to sit.

64
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:40,800
I'll order and find you later.

65
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:47,440
Hi, two noodles.

66
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:50,240
Plus two ribs and two eggs.

67
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:51,640
Two ribs and two eggs.

68
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:53,560
NAME: DUAN SHENGYANG

69
00:05:58,120 --> 00:05:59,760
We haven't done this in so long.

70
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,360
Have you recovered?

71
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:05,720
By the way,

72
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:08,720
Ms. Cheng is no longer
advising undergraduates,

73
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:11,000
or you could have chosen her.

74
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:12,320
Fu Yu,

75
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:14,520
just say what is on your mind.

76
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:16,320
Zheng Yu.

77
00:06:17,840 --> 00:06:19,840
We've been friends for nearly two years,

78
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:22,160
but I just realized when ordering

79
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:24,920
that I don't know your food preferences.

80
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:25,840
I'm not picky.

81
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:30,280
My study abroad plans are set.

82
00:06:30,360 --> 00:06:32,320
I'll go check out housing in advance.

83
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:36,800
After all, finding a nice place
to live isn't easy.

84
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:45,880
Wasn't that girl your partner
in the Excellence Cup?

85
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:53,560
- Is that her boyfriend?
- No.

86
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:57,360
He's probably from
the College of Foreign Languages.

87
00:06:57,440 --> 00:07:00,040
She occasionally takes translation gigs.

88
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:03,800
You two sound close.

89
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:06,880
When did you get so nosy?

90
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:08,520
I've always been nosy.

91
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:12,640
I remember when you first joined
Ms. Cheng's lab.

92
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:17,400
Gosh, hordes of underclassmen
came to the lab to apply to do odd jobs.

93
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:20,720
Unfortunately, you have a heart of iron.

94
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:24,240
Nobody could survive
your ice-cold attitude.

95
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:28,480
So we already agreed.

96
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:30,920
Don't go back on your word.

97
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:31,920
Come on Thursday.

98
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:48,440
Slow down. I haven't started talking yet.

99
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:52,600
- Go on.
- I have good news.

100
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:54,840
Our boss, Professor Qiu Xingping,

101
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,320
might contact you soon.

102
00:07:57,400 --> 00:08:00,000
We're short-staffed for a lab project.

103
00:08:00,080 --> 00:08:01,000
I recommended you.

104
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:03,360
He knows you won the grand prize
in the Excellence Cup.

105
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:05,280
He's very interested in you.

106
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:06,840
What is the research topic?

107
00:08:06,920 --> 00:08:07,760
I've emailed you.

108
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:14,840
Just the basics.
I can't send you the rest yet.

109
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:19,440
Two juniors were working on it,
but they haven't gotten anywhere.

110
00:08:20,120 --> 00:08:22,160
Our boss is very strict.

111
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:25,360
One of the juniors caved
under the pressure and quit.

112
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:26,440
We're short-staffed.

113
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:28,720
Don't worry.

114
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:30,040
If you do take over,

115
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:33,080
you gain experience,
whether you publish a paper or not.

116
00:08:33,799 --> 00:08:35,159
I'm not worried.

117
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:37,600
We have to choose an advisor
this semester.

118
00:08:37,679 --> 00:08:40,960
It's worth treating
as a graduation thesis.

119
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:46,560
Still, thank you
for telling me this in advance

120
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:49,600
and looking out for opportunities
over the past two years.

121
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:52,760
It's nothing. Things are tough for you.

122
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:59,600
A classmate went
to this year's charity bazaar.

123
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:02,880
I never dreamed
your situation was like that.

124
00:09:06,040 --> 00:09:08,520
If you have any problems,
come to me. I can help.

125
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,560
I can handle it myself.

126
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:33,440
I guessed you might be here.

127
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:37,280
I'm helping a client with their homework.

128
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:39,720
My laptop is too slow.

129
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:42,160
Why did you leave so quickly
after eating lunch?

130
00:09:42,240 --> 00:09:43,760
You were gone in a blink.

131
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,600
I'm in a rush to get this done.

132
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:50,200
So I was right.

133
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:51,520
You did see me.

134
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,160
Why didn't you say hi?

135
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:56,080
You seemed busy.

136
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:10,920
Zheng Yu,

137
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:12,480
something's wrong.

138
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:16,400
How so?

139
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:18,720
Why won't you look at me?

140
00:10:20,160 --> 00:10:21,560
Says who?

141
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:42,920
The girl who had lunch with me was Fu Yu.

142
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,800
She's in Ms. Cheng's lab.

143
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:46,400
She got a nice offer

144
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:48,000
and will study in the US soon.

145
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:50,680
I owe her a favor,

146
00:10:50,760 --> 00:10:53,320
so I agreed to go
to her celebration party tomorrow.

147
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:55,920
What favor?

148
00:10:59,040 --> 00:10:59,960
She saved my life.

149
00:11:00,040 --> 00:11:01,280
The meeting is tomorrow.

150
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:03,320
I'll do as much as I can today.

151
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:05,880
I bet someone else is
working harder than me.

152
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:08,680
You're asking who it is?
Who else could it be?

153
00:11:13,520 --> 00:11:14,680
Yanzhou.

154
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:16,640
Yanzhou!

155
00:11:23,200 --> 00:11:24,120
Why are you so quiet?

156
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:29,720
I only knew that you left the lab
due to health reasons.

157
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:33,200
I didn't realize it was so serious.

158
00:11:36,680 --> 00:11:39,000
There is still a lot
you don't know about me.

159
00:11:40,920 --> 00:11:43,120
Then if there's a chance in the future,

160
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:45,640
you can tell me more.

161
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:03,800
All right.

162
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:29,640
Thank you.

163
00:12:32,320 --> 00:12:33,880
Zheng Yu.

164
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:36,240
What are you so happy about?

165
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:37,920
Nothing.

166
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:40,320
Nothing?

167
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:42,640
Try this.

168
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:48,080
Take more.

169
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:55,360
"Qian Yiwen"?

170
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:56,640
Who is that?

171
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:58,560
A regular client of mine.

172
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:00,600
I have to bring this to her tomorrow.

173
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:12,640
I just finished here. I'm on my way now.

174
00:13:14,520 --> 00:13:16,720
Second floor, right-hand side, first room.

175
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:19,200
Okay, got it.

176
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:26,440
Let's congratulate Fu Yu
on securing an acceptance offer!

177
00:13:26,520 --> 00:13:27,960
SCIENTIFIC RESEARCH SUPERSTAR!

178
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:29,600
Thank you, everyone.

179
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:32,840
Even as undergraduates,
I knew this day would come for Fu Yu.

180
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:35,000
That's why…

181
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:37,000
- I prepared…
- What is it?

182
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:38,360
LIKE A RIVER SURGING EAST

183
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:42,880
No, that's embarrassing! Put it away!

184
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:44,680
- How is it embarrassing?
- It is.

185
00:13:44,760 --> 00:13:47,160
We're your undergraduate classmates
and labmates.

186
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:48,920
We're all friends here.

187
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,720
Then why wait? Let's get started!

188
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:53,960
Wait. I'm waiting for one more person.

189
00:13:54,040 --> 00:13:55,320
- Who?
- Who?

190
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:56,440
- So important.
- Right.

191
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:57,920
They're here.

192
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:00,360
Hello.

193
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,280
Hello.

194
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,680
Gu Minghan?

195
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:06,280
Why are you here?

196
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:08,960
Fu Yu, you're such a terrible friend.

197
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:11,320
We had four years together
as undergraduates

198
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:13,120
and three years in the same lab.

199
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:15,000
- Him?
- Seven years of friendship.

200
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:17,440
But she actually forgot to invite me.

201
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:19,920
Fu Yu,

202
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:21,520
did I slip your mind,

203
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:23,360
or did you not intend to invite me?

204
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:25,360
No.

205
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:27,880
Sorry, there was traffic.

206
00:14:33,560 --> 00:14:34,920
Looks like

207
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:36,640
it was a choice.

208
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:39,800
Anyway, you're here already,
so have a seat.

209
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:41,280
- Come.
- Come on, sit.

210
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:42,960
Sit. I'll ask them for a chair.

211
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:45,480
By the way, add another two dozen beers.

212
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,880
I think this really suits you.

213
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:58,560
- Right?
- Yes. Where?

214
00:14:58,640 --> 00:14:59,920
Right…

215
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:01,360
I printed your paper.

216
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:04,960
I knew you were reliable.

217
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:06,880
Calculate the total for the homework,

218
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:09,120
delivery, and printing, and message me.

219
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,440
Okay.

220
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:13,960
Don't leave. We ordered
too much food. Join us.

221
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:16,440
No, thanks.

222
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:18,560
These are all potential clients.

223
00:15:18,640 --> 00:15:21,280
Don't miss out on this opportunity.

224
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:28,040
Waiter, add a place setting.

225
00:15:28,120 --> 00:15:29,360
Okay.

226
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:33,200
Top schools seem out of reach,

227
00:15:33,280 --> 00:15:35,560
but ordinary schools
might be unaffordable.

228
00:15:35,640 --> 00:15:37,720
Competition will be fierce
for a full ride.

229
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:40,800
Our school seems to be promoting
a Sino-German collaboration.

230
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:44,280
There's a grant to study
in a master's program in Germany.

231
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:46,880
Darn, I was born too early!

232
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:47,880
I know, right?

233
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:49,720
Why do you say that?

234
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:52,320
Folks, let me state my personal stance.

235
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:54,640
I'm not studying in Germany.

236
00:15:55,520 --> 00:15:57,920
- Good grief.
- Do you get to be choosy?

237
00:15:58,520 --> 00:16:00,840
Fu Yu, don't worry.
I won't defer another year.

238
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:02,960
Taking an extra year isn't anything bad.

239
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:05,720
Some people are perfectly fine
after taking a year off.

240
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:11,360
Some take time off for their health.

241
00:16:11,440 --> 00:16:12,760
But a deferral could be

242
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:15,800
a sign of a problem
with someone's capability and attitude.

243
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:17,320
Here, Yanzhou.

244
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:24,680
Yanzhou, why do you look so gloomy?

245
00:16:24,760 --> 00:16:26,160
Fu Yu was accepted.

246
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:28,680
- Aren't you happy?
- Gu Minghan.

247
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:30,600
Yanzhou has a great poker face.

248
00:16:30,680 --> 00:16:32,600
That makes it hard to be friends,

249
00:16:32,680 --> 00:16:34,160
but it's perfect for a researcher.

250
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:35,760
Yes, that's right.

251
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:38,320
Back then, he was always in the lab

252
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:40,040
and didn't hang out with us.

253
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:42,520
It really annoyed me.

254
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:43,800
But thinking back on it,

255
00:16:43,880 --> 00:16:46,760
I guess I was annoyed at myself, not him.

256
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:48,960
You were annoyed at yourself!

257
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,200
Come on, let's drink.

258
00:16:51,280 --> 00:16:53,160
- Okay, come on.
- All right! Cheers!

259
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:56,280
To these past few years
of staying true to ourselves.

260
00:16:56,360 --> 00:16:57,200
- Yes!
- Okay!

261
00:16:57,280 --> 00:16:58,120
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

262
00:16:58,200 --> 00:17:00,880
Yanzhou got into the lab
thanks to his brother.

263
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:04,400
Of course he would be
too ashamed to drink with us.

264
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:08,040
Gu Minghan, mind your words.

265
00:17:08,119 --> 00:17:09,520
What's wrong?

266
00:17:09,599 --> 00:17:12,160
Wasn't Zhou Guanqi
the reason that Ms. Cheng…

267
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:16,880
treats Yanzhou so well?

268
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:19,119
That's what is said
in the forum. See for--

269
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:22,720
If that were true,
wouldn't she let him back into the lab?

270
00:17:23,839 --> 00:17:26,920
I suppose it's because he didn't
get anywhere for three years.

271
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,560
Did you come to cause trouble?

272
00:17:28,640 --> 00:17:31,240
- No.
- Excuse me. I'm going to the restroom.

273
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:36,720
Look at you.

274
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:39,040
Guilty conscience.

275
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:41,240
Just give it a rest.

276
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,600
Yanzhou,

277
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:51,800
I'm sorry.

278
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:56,560
I know Gu Minghan had a problem
with you back in the lab.

279
00:17:57,360 --> 00:18:00,120
His attitude has always been problematic.

280
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:02,560
- So I didn't plan to invite him--
- It's fine.

281
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:07,920
I just wanted a get-together
before I left.

282
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,360
I didn't expect…

283
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:10,800
I'm the problem.

284
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:16,160
In any case, congratulations, Fu Yu.

285
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:30,400
I'm full. I'll get going.

286
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:32,920
Do you have to be so transparent?

287
00:18:33,760 --> 00:18:35,040
Thank you.

288
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:37,040
Go on.

289
00:18:41,440 --> 00:18:43,960
Coming from her, the words "thank you"

290
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:45,120
sound so mushy.

291
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:48,800
He looks down his nose at us.

292
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:50,720
Why couldn't he return to the lab?

293
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:53,280
Because Chen Yanzhou couldn't
get anything done.

294
00:18:53,360 --> 00:18:55,360
He's already amazing for an undergrad.

295
00:18:55,440 --> 00:18:57,520
Come on, let's wash your face
and sober up.

296
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:59,360
- He thinks he's his brother.
- Go on.

297
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:02,520
Listen, I was in the same graduating class
as his brother.

298
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:05,840
Be it capability or EQ,
his brother was far better than him.

299
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:09,400
But his brother lost in one aspect.

300
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:11,200
His fate.

301
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:13,040
Just drop it already.

302
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:17,400
Buddy, have you ever heard of
vanishing twin syndrome?

303
00:19:17,480 --> 00:19:21,360
It's when two fetuses
share a single circulatory system.

304
00:19:21,440 --> 00:19:23,840
The one that dies
gets absorbed and replaced

305
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:25,040
by the surviving one.

306
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:27,280
Him! Why did he apply
to Qing Yi University?

307
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:28,600
Why study biology?

308
00:19:28,680 --> 00:19:30,680
And why join our lab?

309
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:33,960
Because he is completely absorbing
and replacing his brother.

310
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:35,480
What is this nonsense?

311
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:37,000
You don't get it.

312
00:19:37,080 --> 00:19:39,640
Everyone in our year knows.

313
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:41,080
Zhou Guanqi

314
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:43,400
died because of Chen Yanzhou.

315
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:47,120
That's all I'll say. It's absolutely--

316
00:19:49,560 --> 00:19:50,640
What the hell!

317
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:53,520
What are you doing?

318
00:19:53,600 --> 00:19:55,360
You want to leave after doing that?

319
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:56,360
That's enough.

320
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:57,880
Who are you?

321
00:20:00,840 --> 00:20:02,120
You again.

322
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:03,520
You want to meddle?

323
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:05,040
- Enough.
- Enough, stop it.

324
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:06,720
Don't throw a drunken fit.

325
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:07,920
I…

326
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:09,040
I'm not drunk.

327
00:20:09,840 --> 00:20:12,560
Fu Yu, it's good that you're here.
Let me ask you.

328
00:20:12,640 --> 00:20:15,120
Why didn't you invite me
to your celebration party?

329
00:20:15,200 --> 00:20:17,360
I've known her for seven years!
Seven years!

330
00:20:17,440 --> 00:20:18,560
Sorry, that's my bad.

331
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:21,120
I forgot. I'll order
whatever you like, okay?

332
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:23,720
- Yes, let's order more.
- I don't want that.

333
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:25,600
- Let's eat. Go.
- She said she forgot.

334
00:20:25,680 --> 00:20:28,320
- What does she mean by that?
- Yanzhou, I'm sorry.

335
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:58,680
Your house is that way.

336
00:20:58,760 --> 00:21:00,360
I'm going back to campus.

337
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:02,480
Zheng Yu.

338
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:09,680
What happened just now?

339
00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:14,600
That person said the wrong thing.

340
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:17,480
What did he say?

341
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:25,640
I can guess even if you don't say.

342
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:29,680
What he said

343
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:32,680
is true.

344
00:21:46,400 --> 00:21:47,920
I already called a cab.

345
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,320
It will be here soon.

346
00:21:50,480 --> 00:21:51,720
Yanzhou.

347
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:54,640
I'll go with you.

348
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:10,720
Are you ditching your research
to come with me because it's my birthday?

349
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:13,720
You're overthinking it.

350
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:16,160
I would've come
even if it wasn't your birthday.

351
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:19,680
Think of it this way.
I get to take a break thanks to you.

352
00:22:27,680 --> 00:22:29,240
It's a long drive.

353
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:30,880
Why don't I quiz you?

354
00:22:32,640 --> 00:22:33,760
If you get it right,

355
00:22:33,840 --> 00:22:35,440
then when we get to the garden,

356
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:38,920
I'll loudly call myself an idiot
in front of all your classmates.

357
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:42,040
Childish.

358
00:22:45,600 --> 00:22:46,440
What topic?

359
00:22:47,800 --> 00:22:48,760
Let me think.

360
00:22:50,760 --> 00:22:52,880
Cristiano Ronaldo's full name.

361
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:55,440
I don't even like football.

362
00:23:03,400 --> 00:23:04,560
You can't look it up.

363
00:23:05,400 --> 00:23:06,400
Guanqi.

364
00:23:07,200 --> 00:23:08,080
Are you cheating?

365
00:23:09,720 --> 00:23:10,960
Guanqi!

366
00:23:12,280 --> 00:23:13,480
FIELD TRIP GROUP

367
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:15,200
AN URGENT NOTICE FROM THE SCHOOL!

368
00:23:15,280 --> 00:23:17,240
DUE TO BAD WEATHER AND SAFETY CONCERNS,

369
00:23:17,320 --> 00:23:19,960
TODAY'S FIELD TRIP
TO THE NANSHAN BOTANICAL GARDEN

370
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:21,200
HAS BEEN CANCELED.

371
00:23:33,360 --> 00:23:37,280
Her child has been traumatized,
but even though she's his mother,

372
00:23:37,360 --> 00:23:39,800
she has been hiding
in her room for so long.

373
00:23:40,640 --> 00:23:43,160
What is up with that?

374
00:23:43,240 --> 00:23:44,200
Mom,

375
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:46,040
Ailan

376
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:48,880
has just laid Guanqi to rest.

377
00:23:50,200 --> 00:23:52,320
Ailan needs some time.

378
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:54,280
What was she doing?

379
00:23:55,280 --> 00:23:58,880
She promised to take Yanzhou there.

380
00:23:58,960 --> 00:24:02,960
If she had gone,
nothing would have happened to Xiaoqi.

381
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:07,040
I will pretend I didn't hear that.

382
00:24:07,120 --> 00:24:09,800
It wasn't Ailan's fault.

383
00:24:09,880 --> 00:24:11,760
Then whose fault was it?

384
00:24:11,840 --> 00:24:13,120
Yanzhou's?

385
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:16,160
If his mom hadn't let him down,

386
00:24:16,240 --> 00:24:17,560
he wouldn't have…

387
00:24:18,320 --> 00:24:19,880
No, Mom.

388
00:24:19,960 --> 00:24:21,560
It's not Yanzhou's fault.

389
00:24:21,640 --> 00:24:23,640
None of them are to blame.

390
00:24:23,720 --> 00:24:27,200
Even now, I still don't know
how any of this happened.

391
00:24:31,800 --> 00:24:33,560
Huaguang,

392
00:24:33,640 --> 00:24:37,800
when I think about how young Xiaoqi was…

393
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:43,640
Who can return Xiaoqi to us?

394
00:24:52,680 --> 00:24:54,160
At the time,

395
00:24:54,240 --> 00:24:56,960
everyone wanted to find
someone to blame for the incident.

396
00:24:58,280 --> 00:25:01,640
So my grandma blamed my mom.

397
00:25:02,400 --> 00:25:04,000
My dad blamed the driver.

398
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:06,680
My aunt went to the school

399
00:25:07,480 --> 00:25:09,880
and asked them
why they sent the notice so late.

400
00:25:11,920 --> 00:25:13,680
And you

401
00:25:13,760 --> 00:25:14,640
blamed yourself.

402
00:25:21,480 --> 00:25:23,400
Do you know why Fu Yu

403
00:25:24,120 --> 00:25:25,600
looks out for me…

404
00:25:28,800 --> 00:25:31,400
and even invited me
to her celebration party?

405
00:25:32,160 --> 00:25:33,160
Why?

406
00:25:36,600 --> 00:25:38,720
She and Guanqi were undergrad classmates.

407
00:25:39,360 --> 00:25:41,640
They knew each other for less than a year…

408
00:25:43,800 --> 00:25:45,240
but she liked him a lot.

409
00:25:46,960 --> 00:25:49,160
This is what she told me

410
00:25:49,240 --> 00:25:51,240
after I joined the lab.

411
00:25:51,320 --> 00:25:52,160
Her own words.

412
00:25:54,480 --> 00:25:55,760
Not just her.

413
00:25:56,800 --> 00:26:00,440
Whether it's Li Yanan or Professor Cheng,

414
00:26:00,520 --> 00:26:03,600
a large part of their tolerance
and patience with me

415
00:26:03,680 --> 00:26:05,720
comes from the regret they feel
about my brother.

416
00:26:07,520 --> 00:26:09,360
If even they are like this,

417
00:26:09,440 --> 00:26:11,560
it's even more so with my family.

418
00:26:13,360 --> 00:26:18,240
How can I compensate everyone
for the loss of such a wonderful person?

419
00:26:19,480 --> 00:26:21,000
I don't know how.

420
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:27,240
ELEGANT CHAMBER OF FRAGRANT ORCHIDS

421
00:26:27,320 --> 00:26:29,160
<i>For example, I learned calligraphy.</i>

422
00:26:29,240 --> 00:26:31,360
<i>Many asked me why I chose the Zhao style.</i>

423
00:26:31,440 --> 00:26:32,960
CHEN YANZHOU

424
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:37,360
I remember Yanzhou was
a picky eater as a child.

425
00:26:37,440 --> 00:26:40,240
He wouldn't even touch
scrambled eggs with tomatoes.

426
00:26:40,840 --> 00:26:43,440
I'm allergic to eggs.
I took some allergy meds for it recently.

427
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:45,400
At your house last time,

428
00:26:45,480 --> 00:26:47,080
you seemed to love the scrambled eggs.

429
00:26:47,160 --> 00:26:49,640
<i>- Favorite dish?</i>
<i>- Scrambled eggs with tomatoes.</i>

430
00:26:49,720 --> 00:26:50,720
Ms. Zhou,

431
00:26:50,800 --> 00:26:53,000
you usually say you don't like crowds.

432
00:26:53,080 --> 00:26:55,200
<i>I'm used to calling my mother Ms. Zhou.</i>

433
00:26:58,640 --> 00:26:59,560
You…

434
00:27:02,040 --> 00:27:03,680
That's why you majored in biology

435
00:27:03,760 --> 00:27:05,120
and joined the lab.

436
00:27:08,360 --> 00:27:09,840
I can't think of

437
00:27:09,920 --> 00:27:11,200
what else I can do.

438
00:27:16,440 --> 00:27:18,240
You're so awful to yourself.

439
00:27:21,440 --> 00:27:23,440
I'm perfectly fine, aren't I?

440
00:27:43,960 --> 00:27:45,920
My mom said

441
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:48,360
people feel sorrow because of love.

442
00:27:52,680 --> 00:27:54,080
Chen Yanzhou,

443
00:27:55,280 --> 00:27:57,560
stop beating yourself up when you're sad.

444
00:27:58,640 --> 00:28:01,200
Doing so is a betrayal of that love.

445
00:28:34,480 --> 00:28:37,440
NANSHAN BOTANICAL GARDEN

446
00:28:39,640 --> 00:28:40,800
<i>My mom said</i>

447
00:28:41,640 --> 00:28:44,600
<i>people feel sorrow because of love.</i>

448
00:28:45,640 --> 00:28:47,000
<i>Chen Yanzhou,</i>

449
00:28:47,520 --> 00:28:50,480
<i>stop beating yourself up when you're sad.</i>

450
00:28:51,440 --> 00:28:53,560
<i>Doing so is a betrayal of that love.</i>

451
00:29:12,440 --> 00:29:13,320
Do you need something?

452
00:29:15,120 --> 00:29:16,160
It's hot.

453
00:29:16,240 --> 00:29:17,280
Thank you.

454
00:29:25,760 --> 00:29:27,480
What is so hard to say?

455
00:29:31,720 --> 00:29:33,120
Mr. Li,

456
00:29:33,200 --> 00:29:36,280
last time, you mentioned
a research institute opportunity.

457
00:29:36,360 --> 00:29:39,440
What documents are needed to apply?

458
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:42,280
Are you interested?
What's your email address?

459
00:29:43,600 --> 00:29:44,480
Thank you.

460
00:29:44,560 --> 00:29:46,920
But it's not for me.

461
00:29:52,840 --> 00:29:53,800
For Chen Yanzhou?

462
00:29:55,600 --> 00:29:57,320
Last time, you said

463
00:29:57,400 --> 00:29:58,280
he was still young

464
00:29:58,360 --> 00:30:00,720
and didn't know that he had other options.

465
00:30:01,440 --> 00:30:03,080
I think

466
00:30:03,160 --> 00:30:05,760
I sort of understand what that means now.

467
00:30:10,120 --> 00:30:11,960
In your eyes,

468
00:30:12,040 --> 00:30:15,600
what was Chen Yanzhou like before?

469
00:30:24,320 --> 00:30:26,400
GAO XING

470
00:30:26,480 --> 00:30:27,680
INCOMING CALL, GAO XING

471
00:30:30,240 --> 00:30:32,480
<i>- Help, it's an emergency.</i>
- What is it?

472
00:30:32,560 --> 00:30:34,960
Look at the math problems I sent you.

473
00:30:35,040 --> 00:30:36,760
Can you help me do them?

474
00:30:36,840 --> 00:30:39,760
<i>I searched all morning</i>
<i>and only found the answers.</i>

475
00:30:39,840 --> 00:30:41,280
<i>The work isn't shown.</i>

476
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:49,000
Stop wasting data.

477
00:30:49,080 --> 00:30:51,960
<i>It's fine. I have unlimited data.</i>

478
00:30:52,600 --> 00:30:55,200
Who gave you the guts
to ask me to do your homework?

479
00:30:55,800 --> 00:30:56,920
Renminbi.

480
00:31:01,800 --> 00:31:03,840
RED PACKET

481
00:31:03,920 --> 00:31:05,840
You have 30 seconds to recall that.

482
00:31:06,520 --> 00:31:08,040
<i>Help me out.</i>

483
00:31:08,120 --> 00:31:09,200
<i>Please.</i>

484
00:31:09,280 --> 00:31:10,960
Twenty-five seconds.

485
00:31:11,040 --> 00:31:12,680
If you don't recall it,

486
00:31:12,760 --> 00:31:14,760
I'll send your mom a screenshot.

487
00:31:14,840 --> 00:31:18,120
GAO XING RECALLED A MESSAGE

488
00:31:29,920 --> 00:31:31,520
What's up?

489
00:31:31,600 --> 00:31:33,960
Stone-cold rejection.

490
00:31:34,040 --> 00:31:35,840
Who did you ask?

491
00:31:35,920 --> 00:31:36,960
My private tutor.

492
00:31:38,040 --> 00:31:40,440
No wonder. No teacher
does homework for students.

493
00:31:41,240 --> 00:31:43,400
Mr. Huang has it out for me.

494
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:45,280
This workbook's problems

495
00:31:45,360 --> 00:31:48,120
could be the hardest questions
on a monthly exam.

496
00:31:48,200 --> 00:31:50,640
I haven't solved any
after staring at it all day.

497
00:31:50,720 --> 00:31:51,840
Why pick on you?

498
00:31:52,600 --> 00:31:54,840
He thinks I'm holding back the class.

499
00:31:55,560 --> 00:31:56,520
Let me take a look.

500
00:31:57,440 --> 00:31:58,280
Forget it.

501
00:31:58,880 --> 00:32:00,360
Why? Afraid I can't solve any?

502
00:32:01,120 --> 00:32:02,000
You'll be stumped.

503
00:32:09,960 --> 00:32:12,280
Gao Xing, I'll show you where to look.

504
00:32:12,360 --> 00:32:13,640
Over there.

505
00:32:14,360 --> 00:32:15,960
I'll leave it here for you.

506
00:32:19,560 --> 00:32:21,200
YEAR 2, CLASS 8

507
00:32:41,280 --> 00:32:44,280
What are you looking at?
I'm here to give you business.

508
00:32:44,360 --> 00:32:45,640
What subject?

509
00:32:45,720 --> 00:32:46,840
Math.

510
00:32:49,360 --> 00:32:51,360
Isn't your usual rate 50 yuan per subject?

511
00:32:51,440 --> 00:32:53,200
I'll pay you double.

512
00:32:54,400 --> 00:32:55,400
Triple is fine too.

513
00:32:58,760 --> 00:33:00,000
What's the matter?

514
00:33:00,080 --> 00:33:02,480
Don't tell me
you want to help me for free.

515
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:07,520
Does your private tutor know

516
00:33:07,600 --> 00:33:09,480
you're paying someone to do your work?

517
00:33:10,000 --> 00:33:11,600
How do you know I have a tutor?

518
00:33:15,640 --> 00:33:18,520
Did you secretly ask around about me?

519
00:33:27,200 --> 00:33:29,600
Don't leave. Let's talk it out.

520
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:33,880
Where did you buy that?

521
00:33:34,560 --> 00:33:36,720
My tutor gave it to me.

522
00:33:36,800 --> 00:33:39,040
We picked them when we went to the beach.

523
00:33:41,880 --> 00:33:42,960
Quadruple.

524
00:33:43,600 --> 00:33:44,840
What?

525
00:33:44,920 --> 00:33:46,920
Quadruple the rate to do your homework.

526
00:33:47,520 --> 00:33:48,400
You…

527
00:33:50,240 --> 00:33:52,360
Fine, quadruple it is.

528
00:33:52,960 --> 00:33:55,400
Add me on WeChat. I'll send the deposit.

529
00:34:01,160 --> 00:34:02,760
Can you get it done this week?

530
00:34:04,160 --> 00:34:06,000
No. You have to wait in line.

531
00:34:07,440 --> 00:34:08,280
Wait in line?

532
00:34:08,360 --> 00:34:10,920
Haven't you ever heard
that the customer is king?

533
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:12,760
A customer who pays quadruple

534
00:34:12,840 --> 00:34:14,880
is practically a god.

535
00:34:14,960 --> 00:34:16,000
I'm talking to you.

536
00:34:16,080 --> 00:34:17,679
Are you listening?

537
00:34:23,679 --> 00:34:25,400
Are you three going out?

538
00:34:25,480 --> 00:34:28,120
No, all four of us are going out.

539
00:34:28,840 --> 00:34:31,639
Zheng Yu, are you
joining Qiu Xingping's lab?

540
00:34:32,480 --> 00:34:33,520
You're well-informed.

541
00:34:34,320 --> 00:34:37,199
Linlin and I heard
when we inquired about postgrad studies.

542
00:34:37,280 --> 00:34:38,199
So is it true?

543
00:34:39,560 --> 00:34:41,639
I received an email from the lab today.

544
00:34:42,560 --> 00:34:44,960
- Congratulations!
- Congratulations!

545
00:34:45,040 --> 00:34:46,719
I'm not sure if it's a good thing.

546
00:34:46,800 --> 00:34:49,600
It's a difficult research topic.

547
00:34:49,679 --> 00:34:50,719
I hope it goes well.

548
00:34:51,520 --> 00:34:52,480
Who cares?

549
00:34:52,560 --> 00:34:54,360
Change is progress.

550
00:34:54,440 --> 00:34:55,560
Progress

551
00:34:55,639 --> 00:34:57,440
means we should celebrate.

552
00:34:57,520 --> 00:34:58,880
So we plan to…

553
00:35:03,040 --> 00:35:04,080
Sorry, one moment.

554
00:35:06,880 --> 00:35:07,800
Hello?

555
00:35:09,640 --> 00:35:11,840
I'm at my dorm. Go ahead.

556
00:35:13,240 --> 00:35:15,240
Change the water for your thale cress?

557
00:35:16,200 --> 00:35:17,760
Is it just changing the water?

558
00:35:18,480 --> 00:35:20,200
Changing the water? Who is that?

559
00:35:21,320 --> 00:35:24,680
If my guess is correct,
it should be Chen Yanzhou.

560
00:35:24,760 --> 00:35:26,200
Chen Yanzhou?

561
00:35:26,280 --> 00:35:29,280
Him again? He wouldn't even
give me a bottle of water.

562
00:35:29,880 --> 00:35:32,560
I know. You've said it before.

563
00:35:32,640 --> 00:35:35,080
H… Have I?

564
00:35:35,160 --> 00:35:36,480
I can confirm. Twice now.

565
00:35:42,480 --> 00:35:43,920
It's nothing.

566
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:46,200
I'll go right away. Don't worry.

567
00:35:47,360 --> 00:35:49,800
Where are you going?
Aren't we going to celebrate?

568
00:35:50,680 --> 00:35:52,520
It's fine, Zheng Yu. Do your thing.

569
00:35:52,600 --> 00:35:54,440
We can celebrate later.

570
00:35:55,600 --> 00:35:57,080
Okay. My treat then.

571
00:36:30,960 --> 00:36:32,320
You lied to me.

572
00:36:32,400 --> 00:36:35,160
You asked me to change the water
because you'd gone home.

573
00:36:36,920 --> 00:36:39,000
I just wanted to thank you in person.

574
00:36:39,080 --> 00:36:40,600
I forgot to say it last time.

575
00:36:41,960 --> 00:36:43,440
Thank you for comforting me.

576
00:36:46,600 --> 00:36:49,400
Besides, if I left, who would
turn on the lights for you?

577
00:36:50,800 --> 00:36:52,520
I've been here many times.

578
00:36:52,600 --> 00:36:54,320
I'm familiar with the area now.

579
00:36:54,400 --> 00:36:55,640
I could still get there

580
00:36:56,240 --> 00:36:57,920
in the dark with my eyes closed.

581
00:37:02,680 --> 00:37:05,600
The lights seem to have
heard your challenge.

582
00:37:13,440 --> 00:37:14,360
Whatever.

583
00:37:14,440 --> 00:37:16,000
It's one more set of stairs.

584
00:37:16,080 --> 00:37:17,840
I'll just feel my way in the dark.

585
00:37:27,600 --> 00:37:30,000
You said you could do it
with your eyes closed.

586
00:37:30,080 --> 00:37:31,880
Don't forget

587
00:37:31,960 --> 00:37:33,320
to close your eyes.

588
00:37:44,080 --> 00:37:45,160
- Hello.
<i>- Hello.</i>

589
00:37:45,240 --> 00:37:47,440
<i>Your delivery has arrived</i>
<i>outside Sixian Hall.</i>

590
00:37:48,400 --> 00:37:51,360
Please tell the building manager
that it's a bit heavy.

591
00:37:51,440 --> 00:37:52,920
Please help bring it upstairs.

592
00:37:53,000 --> 00:37:54,720
Just leave it outside Room 223.

593
00:37:54,800 --> 00:37:56,280
Thank you.

594
00:37:56,360 --> 00:37:58,600
What did you deliver to my dorm?

595
00:37:59,520 --> 00:38:00,600
Bottled water.

596
00:38:01,360 --> 00:38:02,200
Ten boxes.

597
00:38:06,560 --> 00:38:09,560
Fangli, why did you buy so much water?

598
00:38:09,640 --> 00:38:10,920
I didn't buy it.

599
00:38:12,000 --> 00:38:13,280
Then who did?

600
00:38:14,440 --> 00:38:16,760
The buyer's surname is Chen.

601
00:38:16,840 --> 00:38:20,000
I don't know any Chens.

602
00:38:21,400 --> 00:38:23,920
- Chen Yanzhou?
- Chen Yanzhou?

603
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:26,440
Wait. Why did he buy so much water?

604
00:38:26,520 --> 00:38:28,040
Is… Is he crazy?

605
00:38:29,560 --> 00:38:30,600
I…

606
00:38:31,480 --> 00:38:32,720
think…

607
00:38:33,600 --> 00:38:35,000
I probably

608
00:38:35,080 --> 00:38:36,080
know why.

609
00:38:36,160 --> 00:38:37,000
Why…

610
00:38:37,080 --> 00:38:38,120
I think I know too.

611
00:38:39,480 --> 00:38:41,160
Have you ever heard of a tactic

612
00:38:41,240 --> 00:38:43,040
called the pacification strategy?

613
00:38:43,720 --> 00:38:45,160
It's using peaceful measures

614
00:38:45,240 --> 00:38:48,240
to persuade the opposing party
to support you.

615
00:38:49,440 --> 00:38:50,600
Simply put,

616
00:38:50,680 --> 00:38:52,600
there's no such thing as a free lunch.

617
00:38:52,680 --> 00:38:53,600
Wait.

618
00:38:53,680 --> 00:38:55,920
Why are you two speaking in riddles?

619
00:39:02,080 --> 00:39:03,280
What?

620
00:39:03,360 --> 00:39:04,640
Zheng Yu and Chen Yanzhou?

621
00:39:08,160 --> 00:39:10,720
Ten boxes? Isn't that a bit excessive?

622
00:39:11,960 --> 00:39:13,080
Not at all.

623
00:39:13,160 --> 00:39:14,480
I just hope your roommates

624
00:39:14,560 --> 00:39:16,600
will stop saying bad things about me,

625
00:39:16,680 --> 00:39:18,040
especially in front of you.

626
00:39:22,040 --> 00:39:23,320
Let's go change the water.

627
00:39:26,520 --> 00:39:29,400
Why not change it tomorrow?
It's just a few more hours.

628
00:39:31,800 --> 00:39:33,880
I have something important to do tomorrow.

629
00:39:38,240 --> 00:39:39,320
Let's go.

630
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:54,280
Zheng Yu, right?

631
00:39:55,040 --> 00:39:56,240
- Professor Qiu.
- Come.

632
00:39:56,320 --> 00:39:57,600
Let's go to the lab first.

633
00:39:59,200 --> 00:40:01,680
Have you worked in another lab before?

634
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:02,880
No.

635
00:40:02,960 --> 00:40:05,440
That's okay.
There's a first time for everything.

636
00:40:05,520 --> 00:40:08,240
I've arranged for a second-year
master's student to guide you.

637
00:40:08,320 --> 00:40:09,160
Of course,

638
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:12,480
you can also seek advice
from other upperclassmen.

639
00:40:12,560 --> 00:40:14,080
Once you've found your feet,

640
00:40:14,160 --> 00:40:17,240
you can start doing research
with the other two undergraduates.

641
00:40:17,320 --> 00:40:18,160
Two?

642
00:40:18,240 --> 00:40:21,480
But Shengyang told me that
one of them dropped out.

643
00:40:21,560 --> 00:40:22,560
Yes, they did.

644
00:40:22,640 --> 00:40:24,920
But I found someone else in your major.

645
00:40:25,440 --> 00:40:26,560
A three-person team

646
00:40:26,640 --> 00:40:28,480
makes things less stressful.

647
00:40:29,320 --> 00:40:31,360
You should be familiar with this student.

648
00:40:32,200 --> 00:40:34,280
I'm not familiar with many students.

649
00:40:44,360 --> 00:40:47,120
These two are new additions to our lab.

650
00:40:47,840 --> 00:40:50,000
Chen Yanzhou and Zheng Yu.

651
00:40:51,880 --> 00:40:53,520
Fangyi, take good care of them.

652
00:40:53,600 --> 00:40:55,360
Okay.

653
00:40:55,440 --> 00:40:57,200
Okay, I won't take up your time.

654
00:40:57,840 --> 00:40:59,920
When you have time, exchange WeChat info.

655
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:01,200
Get to know each other.

656
00:41:01,880 --> 00:41:04,680
Also, if you have any questions,
you can come to me now.

657
00:41:04,760 --> 00:41:06,200
I won't be here long.

658
00:41:06,920 --> 00:41:08,240
Just for one hour.

659
00:41:10,880 --> 00:41:12,160
I'm Zhong Fangyi.

660
00:41:13,000 --> 00:41:15,160
Your workspace is over there.

661
00:41:16,200 --> 00:41:17,560
That guy is Bi Dezheng.

662
00:41:17,640 --> 00:41:19,000
He will be your research partner.

663
00:41:19,680 --> 00:41:22,240
He and another student
started on it sophomore year.

664
00:41:22,320 --> 00:41:23,800
Now he's the only one left.

665
00:41:24,400 --> 00:41:26,360
You can find me at my workspace here.

666
00:41:30,440 --> 00:41:31,600
Let's go.

667
00:41:37,840 --> 00:41:39,240
This is…

668
00:41:44,120 --> 00:41:47,080
Can't you see
I'm having a moment of silence

669
00:41:47,160 --> 00:41:48,360
for the baby bacteria?

670
00:41:48,960 --> 00:41:51,640
Baby bacteria?

671
00:41:58,360 --> 00:41:59,880
Five minutes.

672
00:41:59,960 --> 00:42:00,800
It's about time.

673
00:42:01,480 --> 00:42:02,720
Family and friends,

674
00:42:02,800 --> 00:42:04,080
take a step back.

675
00:42:05,120 --> 00:42:06,360
I understand.

676
00:42:06,440 --> 00:42:07,760
I know.

677
00:42:07,840 --> 00:42:09,520
I get it.

678
00:42:12,720 --> 00:42:13,760
Sit.

679
00:42:15,920 --> 00:42:17,040
Sit.

680
00:42:25,080 --> 00:42:26,360
Care for coffee?

681
00:42:32,360 --> 00:42:33,200
Restroom break?

682
00:42:36,520 --> 00:42:37,640
Then I'll go.

683
00:42:58,400 --> 00:43:00,080
Does everyone end up like that

684
00:43:00,760 --> 00:43:02,080
after too long in the lab?

685
00:43:02,960 --> 00:43:04,600
It depends on the person.

686
00:43:04,680 --> 00:43:07,480
At least, I can't imagine you
doing this kind of thing.

687
00:43:13,320 --> 00:43:15,480
By the way, why are you--

688
00:43:15,560 --> 00:43:16,720
Zheng Yu.

689
00:43:25,240 --> 00:43:26,600
Research materials for you.

690
00:43:26,680 --> 00:43:28,240
The screen is hard on the eyes,

691
00:43:28,320 --> 00:43:32,440
so I went to print it for you and ended up
coming back too late to welcome you.

692
00:43:33,200 --> 00:43:34,200
You didn't have to.

693
00:43:35,080 --> 00:43:37,600
I already printed it.
It will be a waste not to use it.

694
00:43:40,200 --> 00:43:42,560
Come find me if you ever need anything.

695
00:43:42,640 --> 00:43:43,480
Wait.

696
00:43:44,080 --> 00:43:45,680
I do have a question.

697
00:43:47,320 --> 00:43:49,760
Then let's go to the break room.

698
00:43:54,520 --> 00:43:57,200
Wasn't that girl your partner
in the Excellence Cup?

699
00:43:57,280 --> 00:43:59,240
- Is that her boyfriend?
- No.

700
00:44:00,280 --> 00:44:02,640
<i>He's probably from</i>
<i>the College of Foreign Languages.</i>

701
00:44:03,280 --> 00:44:05,520
So he's not from
the College of Foreign Languages.
